## Your task
Produce exactly one JSON object that validates against the shared `MeetingTurn`
schema. The meeting manager overrides the identity fields, but validation
requires every field present, so emit a placeholder for each and put your real
turn in the content fields.

Identity fields (emit a placeholder; the manager overrides each):
- `turn_id`: any non-empty string (e.g. `"t"`).
- `turn_index`: any integer.
- `speaker`: any non-empty string (your own player id is fine).
- `turn_kind`: `"{{ turn_kind }}"`.
- `reply_to`: any string or `null`.

Content fields (your actual turn):
- `observations`: any first-hand observation that implicates an accused player —
  e.g. a `saw_player` placing them near the body. Each entry is one of:
  - `{"type": "saw_player", "tick": <int>, "subject": "<player_id>", "room": "<room_id>", "co_present": ["<player_id>", ...]}`
  - `{"type": "completed_task", "tick": <int>, "task_id": "<task_id>", "room": "<room_id>"}`
  - `{"type": "found_body", "tick": <int>, "body_of": "<player_id>", "room": "<room_id>"}`
- `claims`: your contribution. Prefer these when your evidence supports them --
  - `corroboration` -- `{"type": "corroboration", "supports": "<player_id>", "on_tick": <int>, "reason": "<reason>"}`. SECOND an accuser whose case your evidence backs.
  - `accusation`    -- `{"type": "accusation", "against": "<player_id>", "confidence": <0.0..1.0>, "reason": "<reason>"}`. If you hold a fresh implicating observation no one has raised.
  - `alibi`         -- `{"type": "alibi", "subject": "{{ agent_id }}", "from_tick": <int>, "to_tick": <int>, "room": "<room_id>", "evidence": ["<ref>", ...]}`.
- `free_text`: one to two sentences — what you saw and who it points at.

## Constraints
- Only reference ticks, rooms, players, and tasks that appear in your private
  memory or the public transcript above. Made-up identifiers fail validation.
- **Ground every corroboration or accusation in a real observation** — a
  sighting, a contradiction, proximity to the body. Do not back a case you have
  no evidence for; an empty second is as useless as silence. Pass only if you
  recorded nothing relevant.

## Output
Output ONLY the JSON object -- no prose before or after it. Start with `{` and
end with `}`.
